Stop cdp's AAANewMessage() looping on a request with Proxy-Info.

When building an answer, AAANewMessage() mirrors the request's Proxy-Info
AVPs (RFC 6733 6.2). It searched with AAAFindMatchingAVP() starting at the
AVP it had just found, and that search checks its start AVP first, so it
returned the same Proxy-Info forever, cloning it into the answer each time.
Any request with Proxy-Info that cdp answers itself, a DWR for one, sent the
receiver process into a loop until shm ran out; that peer got no more
answers and its watchdog failed.

Continue the search after the AVP just mirrored.

diff --git a/src/modules/cdp/diameter_msg.c b/src/modules/cdp/diameter_msg.c
index 569f21784c..1d4fa8e7c8 100644
--- a/src/modules/cdp/diameter_msg.c
+++ b/src/modules/cdp/diameter_msg.c
@@ -299,10 +299,12 @@ AAAMessage *AAANewMessage(AAACommandCode commandCode,
 
 		msg->res_code = 0;
 		/* mirror all the proxy-info avp in the same order */
-		avp_t = request->avpList.head;
-		while((avp_t = AAAFindMatchingAVP(
-					   request, avp_t, 284, 0, AAA_FORWARD_SEARCH))
-				!= 0) {
+		for(avp_t = request->avpList.head; avp_t; avp_t = avp_t->next) {
+			/* the search starts at, and can return, avp_t itself */
+			avp_t = AAAFindMatchingAVP(
+					request, avp_t, AVP_Proxy_Info, 0, AAA_FORWARD_SEARCH);
+			if(!avp_t)
+				break;
 			if((avp = AAACloneAVP(avp_t, 1)) == 0
 					|| AAAAddAVPToMessage(msg, avp, msg->avpList.tail)
 							   != AAA_ERR_SUCCESS)
